WEBVTT

00:01.280 --> 00:03.520
Never forget your poker face.

00:03.520 --> 00:07.560
With his father's teachings in his heart, the miraculous magician glides through skyscrapers.

00:05.440 --> 00:09.860
Kimi no namida ni kon'na ni koishite'ru
(I love your tears so much)

00:05.440 --> 00:09.860
(Natsu-Iro)

00:07.560 --> 00:09.860
Enter Kaitō Kid!

00:09.860 --> 00:12.480
Today's target is the Golden Eye.

00:12.480 --> 00:15.820
Now, it's show time!

00:15.820 --> 00:20.240
kimi no namida ni kon’na ni koishite’ru

00:15.820 --> 00:20.240
I love your tears so much

00:20.240 --> 00:23.080
Wow This Summer day Summer night

00:23.080 --> 00:26.670
soba de waratteitai yo

00:23.080 --> 00:26.670
I want to laugh by your side

00:34.670 --> 00:38.390
bōhatei atsui sunahama

00:34.670 --> 00:38.390
On a pier on a warm sandy beach

00:38.680 --> 00:43.140
machiwabita kiseki yatto otozureta

00:38.680 --> 00:43.140
The miracle I longed for finally came true

00:45.140 --> 00:48.900
dōka kono mama stay with me

00:45.140 --> 00:48.900
Please, stay with me, just like this

00:49.270 --> 00:52.780
Everything for you, I’ll always think of you

00:55.360 --> 00:59.070
hoshi furu yoru wa koishikute

00:55.360 --> 00:59.070
I miss the nights with shooting stars

00:59.410 --> 01:04.040
negai komete koe no kagiri utau no

00:59.410 --> 01:04.040
I wish and sing with all of my voice

01:05.620 --> 01:09.710
mō tomerarenai my sweet song

01:05.620 --> 01:09.710
I can’t stop my sweet song anymore

01:09.880 --> 01:14.420
nakisō na koe de I love you

01:09.880 --> 01:14.420
In a tearful voice I cry ‘I love you’

01:15.210 --> 01:19.680
koe ni naranai hodo hito o suki ni nari

01:15.210 --> 01:19.680
When you like someone so much that you can’t verbalise it

01:19.680 --> 01:22.260
Wow This Summer day Summer night

01:22.260 --> 01:24.970
nanimo kamo ga takaramono (baby)

01:22.260 --> 01:24.970
Everything’s a treasure (baby)

01:25.270 --> 01:29.600
kimi no egao ga kon’na ni yūki kureru

01:25.270 --> 01:29.600
Your smile gives me so much courage

01:29.940 --> 01:35.230
hakanaku itoshii kono kimochi dakishimete

01:29.940 --> 01:35.230
as I embrace this fleeting love

01:35.360 --> 01:40.160
kimi no yokogao zutto zutto mitsumete’ta

01:35.360 --> 01:40.160
I’ve always, always been watching you from your side.

01:56.670 --> 01:56.720
The Reminiscent Golden Eye

01:56.720 --> 01:56.760
The Reminiscent Golden Eye

01:56.760 --> 01:56.800
The Reminiscent Golden Eye

01:56.800 --> 01:56.840
The Reminiscent Golden Eye

01:56.840 --> 01:56.880
The Reminiscent Golden Eye

01:56.880 --> 01:56.920
The Reminiscent Golden Eye

01:56.920 --> 01:56.970
The Reminiscent Golden Eye

01:56.970 --> 01:57.010
The Reminiscent Golden Eye

01:57.010 --> 01:57.050
The Reminiscent Golden Eye

01:57.050 --> 02:02.050
The Reminiscent Golden Eye

02:18.360 --> 02:19.530
There!

02:19.530 --> 02:20.780
It's him!

02:20.780 --> 02:22.370
Kaitō Kid spotted!

02:22.370 --> 02:23.140
All right!

02:23.140 --> 02:26.150
#1, #2 and #3, follow him! Don't let him get away!

02:27.580 --> 02:32.080
Now, how should I deal with those three crows...

02:34.480 --> 02:36.050
What an <i>amateur</i>.

02:36.050 --> 02:36.050
Hmm?

02:36.050 --> 02:40.880
I heard you were the greatest phantom thief in <i>Japon</i>. What a disappointment.

02:40.880 --> 02:45.410
I don't even have to keep watch for such an illogically old-fashioned fancy dress.

02:46.060 --> 02:49.910
Are you trying to be the Arsène Lupin that our great country admires?

02:49.910 --> 02:52.650
Is this guy French?

02:52.650 --> 02:58.400
Certainly, stealing that jewelled sword from such a heavily guarded museum was an impressive feat.

02:58.400 --> 03:00.800
But I could have done so in half the time.

03:00.800 --> 03:02.030
He's a thief too?!

03:05.510 --> 03:08.410
W-What?! There's another one?!

03:08.410 --> 03:10.300
It's a cat?

03:10.300 --> 03:12.330
My name is Chat Noir.

03:12.330 --> 03:17.620
At 9 PM this coming Sunday I'll enjoy our contest at the Hotel Ocean.

03:18.400 --> 03:19.260
<i>À bientôt</i>!

03:21.170 --> 03:22.930
Hey, wait! Ah...

03:30.520 --> 03:35.800
The French thief Chat Noir declares war on Kaitō Kid in a heist notice!

03:35.800 --> 03:40.420
His target is the Golden Eye, which adorned Marie Antoinette's ring finger.

03:40.420 --> 03:43.680
Will Kid take up the challenge and show up?!

03:44.360 --> 03:46.750
Give it back! I was reading that!

03:47.400 --> 03:53.120
Yesterday, Inspector Nakamori retrieved the jewelled sword splendidly, and Kaitō Kid fled at full speed.

03:53.120 --> 03:55.240
It says his approval rating's dropping.

03:55.250 --> 03:57.130
So what?

03:58.020 --> 04:00.670
It wasn't the jewel I was looking for, after all.

04:00.670 --> 04:03.340
I wonder if that coward Kid'll turn up?

04:05.090 --> 04:08.640
A ring, huh... it's probably not the Big Jewel either.

04:08.640 --> 04:10.770
But if he wants a fight, I'll give him one.

04:10.770 --> 04:14.480
Well, even if he <i>does</i> turn up, I'm sure he'll be beaten.

04:14.480 --> 04:18.110
Hey, since you're Japanese, you should be rooting for Kid.

04:18.110 --> 04:21.820
Dummy, the winners'll be the police, and my dad!

04:21.820 --> 04:24.700
Ah, that's what you meant.

04:44.050 --> 04:44.970
<i>Bonjour</i>.

04:44.970 --> 04:47.010
<i>Bonjour, Monsieur</i> Hakuba.

04:58.400 --> 05:01.570
Oh, so this is it.

05:03.490 --> 05:06.990
A single line of white light amongst golden brown.

05:06.990 --> 05:10.380
It's certainly a ring fit to be named Golden Eye.

05:10.380 --> 05:12.230
Mr. Dan Mitsuishi.

05:12.230 --> 05:19.040
Yes! It's the last one of the seven accessories Antoinette gathered to ward away evil.

05:19.040 --> 05:20.510
The last one?

05:20.510 --> 05:24.170
The other six were all taken by Chat Noir.

05:24.820 --> 05:28.190
And just after a buyer had been found, too.

05:28.190 --> 05:32.850
Then why not leave it locked up in a mansion safe in your country?

05:32.850 --> 05:37.410
Why'd you go and exhibit it at a hotel all the way out here?

05:37.410 --> 05:41.670
It's all a trap to lure out Chat Noir.

05:41.670 --> 05:42.940
A trap?

05:42.940 --> 05:47.940
To put it bluntly, I don't trust any security system except ours.

05:47.940 --> 05:50.100
W-What?!

05:50.100 --> 05:58.250
Of course, trust is out of the question when you lot are made fun of by Kaitō Kid, a single petty thief.

05:59.010 --> 06:01.460
Don't underestimate the Japanese police!

06:01.460 --> 06:05.030
If you leave it to us, there won't be a single outsider in this hotel!

06:05.030 --> 06:06.420
Dad!

06:06.420 --> 06:07.900
Here's your lunch box!

06:08.840 --> 06:11.380
And these outsiders are?

06:11.380 --> 06:16.530
T-They're my daughter, Aoko and her classmate, Kaito Kuroba-<i>kun</i>.

06:16.530 --> 06:18.090
Hmph, okay.

06:18.090 --> 06:21.490
Your weak security is also something I calculated for.

06:21.490 --> 06:23.110
What do you mean?

06:23.110 --> 06:26.730
There's no point to a mousetrap if it doesn't have an entrance.

06:26.730 --> 06:29.150
A mousetrap? D-Don't tell me...

06:29.150 --> 06:32.100
...you intend to capture Kid and Chat Noir?

06:32.100 --> 06:33.070
Take a look at this.

06:44.000 --> 06:45.970
W-What?!

06:45.970 --> 06:49.140
This special glass contains wires of titanium alloy.

06:49.140 --> 06:51.430
It can withstand even a 10 tonne blast.

06:51.430 --> 06:57.350
Furthermore, five minutes before the scheduled time of 9 PM, all lifts will be stopped at this top floor,

06:57.350 --> 06:59.600
and all staircases will be sealed as well.

06:59.600 --> 07:02.430
In other words, after 9 PM, escape is impossible.

07:02.770 --> 07:08.650
Even the hangglider and paraglider they use will be useless white elephants!

07:08.650 --> 07:11.210
I-It's nothing short of amazing.

07:11.210 --> 07:13.260
Yeah... it is.

07:13.260 --> 07:16.160
So it's easy to get in, but hard to get out, huh?

07:16.160 --> 07:21.190
But really, putting such a precious ring in such a cheap case is a bit...

07:21.980 --> 07:29.040
I thought I'd protect the ring with the only alarm system you have that I can trust.

07:29.040 --> 07:31.160
Hmph, so where is it then?

07:31.160 --> 07:33.840
Like I said, it's <i>you</i>, Inspector Nakamori.

07:34.920 --> 07:40.030
You will wear the ring yourself, and sit on that case waiting for them.

07:40.030 --> 07:41.730
M-Me?!

07:41.730 --> 07:46.730
Until the time has passed, if you keep your fist tightly clenched, it can't be stolen.

07:46.730 --> 07:48.110
Hey, is he serious?!

07:48.110 --> 07:52.630
Just in case they try and put you to sleep and take you with it,

07:52.630 --> 07:55.540
I'll have you wear a gas mask and transmitter.

07:56.030 --> 07:59.460
I see. That's a good idea.

07:59.460 --> 08:03.390
So there'll be no way to steal the ring except cutting my finger off.

08:03.390 --> 08:05.710
W-What'll you do if it <i>is</i> cut off?!

08:05.710 --> 08:07.090
Don't be silly!

08:07.090 --> 08:10.030
Kid wouldn't do anything so uncivilised...

08:10.030 --> 08:11.280
But <i>he</i>...

08:12.700 --> 08:14.860
...Chat Noir would not hesitate to.

08:15.550 --> 08:18.430
Hmph... Who are you?

08:18.430 --> 08:23.190
Ah, this is Ruby Jones-<i>san</i>, an investigator from an American insurance company.

08:23.190 --> 08:24.800
Insurance company?

08:24.800 --> 08:33.780
Yes, all of Mr. Dan Mitsuishi's jewels are insured against theft, and since Kid is a disguise expert...

08:33.780 --> 08:35.620
You had your faces checked?

08:35.620 --> 08:37.240
Yes, just to be sure.

08:37.240 --> 08:41.480
This is the way of someone born and raised in Texas.

08:41.480 --> 08:42.900
Don't take it badly.

08:42.900 --> 08:45.200
But why did you come?

08:45.200 --> 08:47.420
The company has been having doubts.

08:47.420 --> 08:53.620
Since each theft required considerable skill, we've been wondering if Chat Noir is your accomplice.

08:53.620 --> 08:54.840
O-Of course not!!

08:54.840 --> 08:59.100
Also, if the Golden Eye's stolen, the company will suffer great losses.

08:59.100 --> 09:03.270
So I was dispatched to defend it by any means necessary.

09:03.270 --> 09:05.680
That's a job for us police...

09:05.680 --> 09:08.480
You will be hurt if you underestimate Chat Noir.

09:08.480 --> 09:14.400
After all, what happened to Mrs. Mitsuishi, who had the Cat's Eye embedded in her hair ornaments?

09:14.450 --> 09:20.070
Chat Noir cut off and took off with all the hair that was woven into her hair ornaments.

09:20.490 --> 09:23.600
Then he'd cut my finger off too...

09:23.600 --> 09:25.160
It's unforgivable!

09:25.810 --> 09:29.630
This time I'll catch that stray cat and cut his life short!

09:29.630 --> 09:31.500
Just watch me...

09:31.500 --> 09:34.960
If you're worried, how about putting the ring on over gloves?

09:35.950 --> 09:37.850
Although it mightn't do you any help.

09:44.130 --> 09:47.260
That woman shows no sympathy to others...

09:47.260 --> 09:52.130
Is this plan really okay?

09:52.130 --> 09:55.320
Didn't you say it was a good idea earlier, Dad?

09:55.320 --> 09:56.980
It's such a nuisance though!

09:56.980 --> 09:59.240
So wrap this loop around your shirt button—

10:00.840 --> 10:05.170
if you don't put it on your shirt button like this then it'll dangle.

10:05.170 --> 10:07.460
Ah, thanks, Kaito-<i>kun</i>.

10:07.510 --> 10:12.750
shiny stone

10:07.510 --> 10:12.750
But really, Mitsuishi and Ruby, they've both got jewel-like names.

10:12.750 --> 10:13.960
Hey!

10:13.960 --> 10:18.300
Isn't the name ‘Aoko’ taken from the ‘blue’ of sapphire too?!

10:18.300 --> 10:25.470
Come to think of it, Ruby-<i>san</i> was named after her birthstone too, just like me.

10:25.470 --> 10:29.510
Why, our birthdays are close, aren't they? Let's be friends!

10:29.510 --> 10:30.960
Ah, sure!

10:30.960 --> 10:33.350
Then, your boyfriend was born in December?

10:33.350 --> 10:35.800
No, Kaito was born in June.

10:35.800 --> 10:38.550
Hmm? Oh, I see.

10:38.550 --> 10:39.650
...was what happened.

10:41.370 --> 10:42.530
Geez...

10:42.530 --> 10:44.700
Dad! Didn't you listen to a thing I said?!

10:47.980 --> 10:53.200
It feels kind of unfair, but oh well, ah well, a contest is a contest.

10:57.400 --> 10:58.640
From overseas?

10:59.300 --> 11:00.420
Hello?

11:00.420 --> 11:02.100
Yo! You're alive, then?

11:02.840 --> 11:05.650
That snobbish sarcastic tone...!

11:05.650 --> 11:09.650
Though I guess since Spider's over here, you don't have to worry.

11:09.650 --> 11:11.120
H-Hakuba?

11:11.120 --> 11:12.900
It's even the talk of Paris.

11:13.510 --> 11:17.340
That the French phantom thief ‘Chat Noir’ challenged you in Japan, that is.

11:17.340 --> 11:18.360
Moron! It wasn't me he challenged, it was Kid—

11:18.360 --> 11:20.530
Moron! It wasn't me he challenged, it was Kid—

11:21.560 --> 11:24.700
W-What did you say? Spider's there?

11:26.470 --> 11:28.210
So then you <i>are</i> interested?

11:29.080 --> 11:36.030
Of course you are, the world's greatest hitman is targeting Kaitō Kid, and that's you.

11:36.030 --> 11:38.280
W-What are you talking about?

11:38.280 --> 11:39.380
Then you won't mind if I catch Spider
while you're still playing dumb?

11:39.380 --> 11:42.530
Then you won't mind if I catch Spider
while you're still playing dumb?

11:42.530 --> 11:43.460
That's...

11:43.460 --> 11:46.210
Oh, don't worry.

11:46.930 --> 11:51.270
I won't catch him until I've
completely exposed his identity.

11:51.270 --> 11:54.390
Like I said, I'm not Kid!

11:55.170 --> 11:56.720
Ah, whatever.

11:56.720 --> 12:01.600
Since I went through the trouble of calling you, I may as well offer you some info I happened upon about Chat Noir.

12:01.600 --> 12:05.250
From what a friend in the Paris police force said, for some reason in recent years

12:05.250 --> 12:09.660
he's stolen nothing but items from Mr. Dan Mitsuishi's Antoinette Collection.

12:10.590 --> 12:18.590
They originally belonged to Dan's father, Mr. Ken Mitsuishi, and had slept in a warehouse for 30 years, but his son dug them out.

12:19.220 --> 12:25.680
Also, the designs of the fakes that Chat Noir leaves behind at crime scenes instead of a signature

12:25.680 --> 12:30.060
are always exactly the same as the item being stolen from the Antoinette Collection.

12:30.060 --> 12:32.610
As if they'd been made from the same plans.

12:32.610 --> 12:34.050
The same plans?

12:34.050 --> 12:35.980
And that's all you're getting from me.

12:35.980 --> 12:38.350
Well, do the best you can.

12:38.350 --> 12:41.940
Oh, the show should start
any moment now. I do apologise.

12:44.380 --> 12:46.820
Hmm, could it be...

12:50.530 --> 12:52.920
Well, for now I better start the plan.

13:02.570 --> 13:03.630
Ah, Jii-<i>chan</i>?

13:04.340 --> 13:07.510
Didn't you say you wanted to visit an opera house once?

13:07.510 --> 13:08.880
Where are you, Kai—?

13:08.880 --> 13:10.470
Aoko-<i>chan</i>.

13:11.160 --> 13:14.280
Kaito-kun said to deliver this to someone called Jii-<i>san</i>.

13:15.310 --> 13:18.330
Did he go home, then?

13:18.330 --> 13:22.650
Really! He's the one who suggested we bring Dad his lunch box!

13:22.650 --> 13:23.690
Sorry, Aoko.

13:23.690 --> 13:27.150
I can't afford to lose this match.

13:33.280 --> 13:34.740
Let's fight, Kid!

13:48.000 --> 13:50.550
Well then, we'll leave it to you, Inspector Nakamori.

13:50.550 --> 13:53.240
Make sure they don't notice the transmitter.

13:54.680 --> 13:55.730
Calm down.

13:55.730 --> 13:58.350
Never mind what I said earlier, it won't be stolen so easily.

13:58.350 --> 14:01.270
I never should've accepted this after all...

14:03.100 --> 14:06.080
W-What? What was that glare...

14:06.520 --> 14:08.920
So, how will you attack, Kid?

14:09.440 --> 14:12.370
I've completed preparations myself...

14:12.860 --> 14:16.760
It's now 8:55. What's the situation?

14:16.760 --> 14:18.700
Everything is going as planned.

14:18.700 --> 14:22.120
The four lifts are all stopped at the top floor.

14:22.120 --> 14:25.040
The staircases down from the roof are also completely sealed.

14:27.020 --> 14:30.670
Is it okay to have even the police helicopters pull out?

14:30.670 --> 14:32.540
I told you.

14:32.540 --> 14:36.380
As long as we have this special glass, both intrusion and escape are impossible.

14:36.380 --> 14:38.010
Helicopters are just a nuisance.

14:39.300 --> 14:41.810
Hey! What're those?

14:41.810 --> 14:43.220
Floodlights!

14:43.220 --> 14:45.900
It's dark in here, so they're to light up the room...

14:45.900 --> 14:47.300
Whose orders?

14:47.300 --> 14:48.150
The inspector's!

14:48.150 --> 14:50.860
Inspector Nakamori, earlier, over the radio!

14:50.860 --> 14:54.360
- Hey, I never...
- There's no time, turn them on!

14:55.400 --> 14:57.820
What?! Fools! If you turn that many on at once...

14:58.910 --> 14:59.410
Oh, crap!

15:00.830 --> 15:02.610
Like I said!

15:02.610 --> 15:06.170
It's fine, the spare generator'll soon restore power.

15:06.170 --> 15:11.760
Besides, I must welcome the foolish petty thieves who have stepped into my trap.

15:11.760 --> 15:12.870
Inspector, the gas mask.

15:14.330 --> 15:16.770
Make sure not to open the hand with the ring on.

15:16.770 --> 15:18.930
Still, with it this dark...

15:18.930 --> 15:20.090
Ah, thanks.

15:21.540 --> 15:23.180
K-Kaitō Kid?!

15:23.180 --> 15:24.430
Protect the inspector!

15:27.250 --> 15:30.010
Let go! That's my face!

15:30.010 --> 15:33.150
I've been waiting for this moment, Kaitō Kid!

15:33.150 --> 15:35.230
H-Hey! Let go!

15:40.960 --> 15:43.560
T-The ring! Is the ring all right?!

15:43.560 --> 15:47.250
Don't worry, I've been holding this hand tightly.

15:47.250 --> 15:48.510
See!

15:48.510 --> 15:50.170
I-Inspector! The jewel!!

15:52.840 --> 15:54.890
I-It's gone?!

15:54.890 --> 15:56.750
Look! It's Kid!

15:57.670 --> 16:00.610
Wasn't it supposed to be impossible to escape?!

16:00.610 --> 16:02.590
Hmph! You underestimated him.

16:02.590 --> 16:07.520
Unlike the stray cats of France, Kid is a great thief who makes the impossible possible!

16:12.520 --> 16:14.360
As you say.

16:14.360 --> 16:16.820
Anyway, for now I'll pursue Kid!

16:16.820 --> 16:19.150
Okay! Us police should too!

16:20.570 --> 16:21.580
Wait.

16:21.580 --> 16:24.220
Leave her to chase that dummy.

16:24.220 --> 16:25.490
Dummy?

16:30.870 --> 16:34.110
Also, we haven't lost yet.

16:34.110 --> 16:35.750
- As the ring is...
- Inspector!

16:36.730 --> 16:40.590
We found this man sleeping in the toilet!

16:40.590 --> 16:42.190
T-That's...?!

16:42.190 --> 16:44.510
That can't be...huh?!

16:44.510 --> 16:47.770
When I think about how composed you've been...

16:47.770 --> 16:49.170
You're Kid in disguise, aren't you?

16:49.780 --> 16:50.430
O-Of course not!

16:50.430 --> 16:51.770
Get him!!

17:00.510 --> 17:04.530
The lifts themselves are covered in the special glass, but...

17:08.620 --> 17:12.500
this is ordinary thick glass.

17:12.500 --> 17:16.420
S-Stop! I'm really me!

17:16.420 --> 17:18.110
Get a medical team, quickly!

17:19.190 --> 17:20.340
Don't tell me...?!

17:22.260 --> 17:23.840
I-Inspector!

17:26.230 --> 17:29.100
Yeah, everything went as planned, Jii-<i>chan</i>.

17:29.100 --> 17:31.180
They fell for it well!

17:31.180 --> 17:35.400
And all I had to do was stick a dummy setting on the back of the ring.

17:37.690 --> 17:40.360
I'm so awesome!

17:43.280 --> 17:45.310
A phone? Whose is it?

17:48.340 --> 17:50.240
Umm... Hello?

17:50.240 --> 17:52.370
<i>Bonsoir</i>, Kaitō Kid.

17:53.320 --> 17:54.540
Chat Noir?!

17:54.540 --> 18:01.380
That you're still there means you're gazing at the ring you stole and smiling, doesn't it?

18:01.380 --> 18:05.180
Without knowing that it's a fake.

18:05.180 --> 18:06.080
A fake?!

18:06.080 --> 18:07.590
Of course!

18:07.590 --> 18:10.730
Did you really think I'd let you wear the real thing?

18:10.730 --> 18:12.270
Then the real one...

18:12.270 --> 18:17.010
See, the real one is in the tiepin connected to your necktie...

18:19.520 --> 18:21.430
W-What?!

18:21.430 --> 18:27.410
Thanks to you turning off the lights, I was able to get the real one.

18:27.410 --> 18:30.560
I thought I'd call to say a brief thanks.

18:31.460 --> 18:35.820
As this was the last item I truly <i>had</i> to obtain.

18:35.820 --> 18:39.250
So you pretended to chase my dummy remote-controlled hangglider

18:39.250 --> 18:45.130
to leave the exhibition hall and escaped by paraglider from the roof.

18:47.200 --> 18:53.600
Isn't that right, you who came here as an investigator for an insurance company, Ruby Jones-<i>san</i>?

18:57.360 --> 18:58.850
How did you know?

18:58.850 --> 19:00.700
Birthstones.

19:00.700 --> 19:01.820
Birthstones?

19:02.480 --> 19:05.250
Why, our birthdays are close, aren't they?

19:06.490 --> 19:08.590
Rubies and sapphires...

19:08.590 --> 19:12.770
True, in France their birthdays
are close, being March and April...

19:12.770 --> 19:15.770
but in America and Japan they're July and September.

19:15.770 --> 19:19.420
So I thought you may be a Frenchwoman pretending to be American.

19:19.420 --> 19:22.700
Oh, you heard that?

19:22.700 --> 19:27.080
By the way, in France, December happens to be Malachite.

19:27.080 --> 19:29.140
It certainly is... Just as I expected from you.

19:29.140 --> 19:30.260
There's one more thing.

19:30.260 --> 19:35.190
I learnt that you were a tragic thief retrieving her father's belongings.

19:35.930 --> 19:39.160
The collection sealed away 30 years ago.

19:39.160 --> 19:43.860
The imitations left at crime scenes suspected to come from the same plans.

19:43.860 --> 19:47.080
Your costume, as if representing your mourning.

19:47.080 --> 19:48.860
It was easy to tell.

19:51.010 --> 19:51.750
Right.

19:54.460 --> 19:59.830
The Antoinette Collection were imitations designed by my father, a jewellery designer,

19:59.830 --> 20:05.860
intended for Mr. Dan Mitsuishi's father, Mr. Ken Mitsuishi, to give to his wife.

20:05.860 --> 20:07.760
But thanks to the skill of the craftmanship,

20:07.760 --> 20:10.600
he announced they were the real things,

20:10.600 --> 20:14.130
and my father's conscience as a craftsman led him to commit suicide in protest.

20:14.130 --> 20:17.510
Ken unwillingly sealed away the collection.

20:17.510 --> 20:21.100
Nevertheless, his moronic son broke the seal.

20:21.100 --> 20:25.520
Just to attract his wife, who loves to live in luxury.

20:25.520 --> 20:29.450
So I became Chat Noir and began to recover them.

20:29.450 --> 20:31.490
The mementos of my father...

20:35.280 --> 20:39.370
Unfortunately, that is a fake that I prepared.

20:44.170 --> 20:48.050
Then, even knowing it was a fake, you still...

20:52.980 --> 20:54.610
I lost.

20:54.610 --> 20:57.550
It seems I have no choice but to give up on it this time.

20:57.550 --> 21:00.980
No, this is a precious item of your father's.

21:00.980 --> 21:02.850
I'll give it back to you in five seconds.

21:02.850 --> 21:05.650
Dummy. Where do you think I am?

21:05.650 --> 21:10.040
Even if you were the genius magician Houdini, there's no way you could...

21:08.440 --> 21:10.570
Three, two...

21:10.570 --> 21:11.490
One...

21:21.400 --> 21:22.920
Why...

21:22.920 --> 21:25.750
Why would you go so far for me...

21:25.750 --> 21:30.840
That's because your reason for commiting crimes rather resembles mine...

21:32.590 --> 21:33.850
So they're finally here?

21:37.490 --> 21:38.600
Ah, there!

21:39.410 --> 21:40.980
Kaitō Kid!

21:42.230 --> 21:43.870
A hole?!

21:43.870 --> 21:46.300
Don't attack him! Lower the lift!

21:46.300 --> 21:47.820
Okay!

21:47.820 --> 21:49.730
You fool! That's not a hole...

21:51.540 --> 21:52.570
Bye-bye.

21:56.600 --> 21:58.240
You're flying again, aren't you.

21:58.240 --> 22:00.980
In that illogically white guise...

22:00.980 --> 22:01.660
Yeah.

22:01.660 --> 22:05.580
As unlike petty thieves dressed in black that hide from people's eyes...

22:05.580 --> 22:09.380
I am the magnificent daredevil, Kaitō Kid!

22:17.850 --> 22:21.970
marakaito

22:17.850 --> 22:21.970
By the way, in France, December happens to be Malachite...

22:23.220 --> 22:23.880
‘Kaito’...

22:24.690 --> 22:27.150
Kaito was born in June.

22:32.550 --> 22:35.490
Goodbye, Kaitō Kid...

22:36.590 --> 22:40.240
<i>Merci, Kaito Kuroba</i>...

22:46.370 --> 22:47.500
Shin’ichi Kudō

22:47.330 --> 22:50.840
Koi ni Koishite
(Falling in love)

22:47.330 --> 22:50.840
(Mai Kuraki)

22:51.840 --> 22:56.510
kimi ni zenzen kyōmi nai uso you are my perfect guy

22:51.840 --> 22:56.510
I’m not interested in you at all — I’m lying, you are my perfect guy

22:57.010 --> 23:01.510
tokimeki wa kakusenai honto wa ki ni natte shikatanai

22:57.010 --> 23:01.510
I can’t hide my beating heart, I’m really into you, I can’t help it

23:02.060 --> 23:06.520
koi ni bukiyō son’na style kimi no mae da to betsujin mitai

23:02.060 --> 23:06.520
I’m no good at love, with a bad style, I become someone else when facing you

23:07.100 --> 23:10.980
dare ni mo ienai himitsu no mama

23:07.100 --> 23:10.980
I don’t tell anyone about it

23:12.110 --> 23:16.070
soredemo I’m alright koi no yukue nante

23:12.110 --> 23:16.070
Still, I’m alright, love just isn’t for me

23:16.400 --> 23:20.370
mada it isn’t the last chance for me

23:16.400 --> 23:20.370
and it still isn’t the last chance for me

23:20.990 --> 23:26.000
iron’na love story o egaite’ru mune no naka

23:20.990 --> 23:26.000
I have many love stories carved into my heart

23:26.160 --> 23:31.290
demo risō ni wa hodo tōi

23:26.160 --> 23:31.290
but they’re far from my ideals

23:31.790 --> 23:36.720
watashi-tte wagamama sore kurai no koto wakatte’ru

23:31.790 --> 23:36.720
I know I’m selfish but…

23:36.880 --> 23:42.850
dakedo nani ka ikenai no?

23:36.880 --> 23:42.850
…is there anything wrong with that?

23:43.510 --> 23:44.930
Edogawa

23:43.510 --> 23:53.150
kimi to no koi ni koi o shite’ru dake de tsutaetakute mo mada

23:43.510 --> 23:53.150
Just being in love with you is enough, I couldn’t confess even if I wanted to…

23:53.480 --> 24:05.950
himitsu ni shite’ru hō ga shiawase dakara ima wa watashi dake no secret love

23:53.480 --> 24:05.950
I’m happier with it being a secret, so for now, it’ll be my secret love

24:00.160 --> 24:06.330
To Conan
Edogawa-<i>kun</i>

24:06.330 --> 24:08.030
It's a holiday, so let's go somewhere!

24:08.030 --> 24:09.480
There's no holidays for detectives!

24:09.480 --> 24:11.170
None for phantom thieves, either...
